comment.narrative:
The Dutch embassy in Maputo (EKN-Map) aims to apply programmatic and systems approach towards local private sector development (PSD) in Mozambique. This PADEO approach focuses on local needs, is inclusive, and aims to enhance the number of small scale food producers (male and female) that progressively realize a living income and/or progressively decrease the yield gap while cultivating an increased hectarage of farm land under at least 2 conservation practices; with a focus on creating income for youth and vulnerable people (YVP). • Small-scale food producers’ farming systems have been chosen as the focus for the PADEO approach in Mozambique. They are also key in the Food and Nutrition security program (F&NS) of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs department Inclusive Good Growth. PADEO aims to improve the enabling environment for small-scale food producers in these systems. As result of this project: leverage points make a link with two key F&NS programs financed by BZ-IGG: AgroVida in Cabo Delgado and Mangwana in the Beira corridor. • Access to knowledge was selected a critical leverage point for PADEO in Mozambique, which will enable making the link with the planned TVET/HE program finanzed by BZ-DSO for Mozambique. The TVET/HE program aims to bring more coherence to the Dutch policy efforts, with education as a means for more impact, with evidence-based programming; and with the involvement of the public sector in the country and a clear role for the private sector. Connection with the TVET/HE program is to be made where opportune (especially in area access to knowledge).
Overall, the project contributes to the development of the PADEO approach in Mozambique, one where systems thinking, programmatic approach and local needs is at the core. The PADEO Mozambique team requested an explicit focus on a single leverage point for the further design of interventions;
The project delivered two system analysis studies, one for Cabo Delgado and one for the Sofala/Berira corridor. Key ouputs of these report
